# These files are AUTHORED ONCE AND SHIPPED TWICE: each copy here and its twin
# in the sibling `birding` repo must stay BYTE-IDENTICAL, which that repo's
# parity suite enforces exactly. Without this, core.autocrlf=true checks one
# copy out as CRLF on Windows while the other stays LF and the twins "drift" by
# hundreds of bytes of pure line ending with zero content difference — a
# failure that looks like a content bug and is not one.
#
# The `birding` repo pins the matching side in its own .gitattributes. Both
# halves are needed: these are SEPARATE checkouts with independent
# core.autocrlf settings, so pinning one repo only narrows the window rather
# than closing it. Adding a shared file means editing both.
www/section-docs.json text eol=lf
www/scope-sites.json text eol=lf
www/travel-zones.json text eol=lf
